{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\n# Review Critic\n\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\n\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\n\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\n\n\n\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\n\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\n\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\n\n\n## User's Initial Request\n\nREVIEW CONTRACT\ntask=MARATHON-7\nattempt=1\nbase=de8f4752941296f0e83ecc0dd9d58036d2b99bdc\ncandidate=7e8e165bda60d4bc84d665c89ace8752e0e7d6bf\n\nDESIGN:\n# MARATHON-7 — Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes channel lifecycle for Huddle on top of the workspace tenancy shipped in MARATHON-5/6: authenticated callers can create public/private channels under a workspace slug, join and leave channels (with open-workspace auto-onboard and invite_only/guest/private gates), list channel members as `UserObj`, patch topic, archive/unarchive (owner-only), and pin/unpin messages. It also implements the SPA-locked workspace join seam (`POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join`) that MARATHON-16 already calls. It locks the `/api/channels/*` and pin REST contracts, introduces migration **v3** (`messages` minimal + `channel_pins`), and exports a shared **archived-write guard** (`423`) that MARATHON-8/11 must reuse.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 3** additive: minimal `messages` + `channel_pins` (pins need message rows; same “schema-ahead” pattern as M5 channels-before-CRUD) |\n| Route layout | (1) Extend `server/workspaces/routes.py`: `POST /{slug}/join`, `POST /{slug}/channels`. (2) New `server/channels/routes.py` prefix `/api/channels`: join, leave, PATCH, members, archive, unarchive, pins. (3) New `server/messages/routes.py` (or pin routes mounted under `/api/messages`) for `POST/DELETE /{id}/pin` |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all new endpoints require Bearer |\n| `ChannelObj` | **Unchanged** key set from MARATHON-5 (`CHANNEL_OBJ_KEYS`); this task owns create/mutate behavior |\n| Workspace join vs channel join | **Both**: SPA uses workspace join (M16); product grader uses channel join with open auto-onboard. Same membership insert helper |\n| Private “invite” | No private-invite table yet (MARATHON-12). “Without invite” ≡ caller lacks `channel_members` row → **403** on join. Creator is auto-member on create; tests may SQL-seed members until add-member API exists |\n| Pins without full Message API | Minimal `messages` table + thin `MessageObj` mapper (empty `files`/`reactions`/`mentions`, `reply_count=0`) so pin list/embed works; MARATHON-8 owns message CRUD and enriches the same object |\n| Archived writes | Shared helper `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; used by topic PATCH + pin mutate now; documented for M8 message/reaction writes |\n| Events / Redis | No pub/sub (MARATHON-13/14); optional no-op hooks OK but not required |\n| Timestamps | Reuse `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) consistent with M3–M6 |\n\n### Why\n\n- Product contract is explicit on paths, envelopes, role matrix, 423, and pin shapes; inventing alternate routes would fail the grader and diverge from SPA settings (MARATHON-17/18).\n- Workspace join is already wired in `static/js/shell.js`; omitting it leaves onboarding broken despite channel-join auto-onboard.\n- Introducing a minimal `messages` table for pins mirrors M5 shipping `channels` early — one migration, stable FKs, no pin→message soft-orphan mess.\n- Centralizing the archived guard prevents M8 from inventing a second 423 code/message.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Only channel-join auto-onboard; skip workspace join | Breaks MARATHON-16 SPA contract already shipped |\n| Defer pins entirely to MARATHON-8 | Task + product contract require pin routes in this task |\n| Pin table without messages; return message stubs | Violates `{pins:[{message,...}]}` and FK integrity |\n| Allow members to create private channels | Product: member → **403** on `is_private:true` |\n| Soft 200 on guest join | Product: guest → **403** |\n| Use `MemberObj` for channel members list | Product: `UserObj[]` under `members` |\n| 404 for archived writes | Product: **423** |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nMinimal `messages` lands before message CRUD. Implementers must not invent message POST here; tests for pins SQL-insert message rows (or a tiny test helper). MARATHON-8 must **extend** v\n\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=7e8e165bda60d4bc84d665c89ace8752e0e7d6bf APPROVED — <reason>\nor\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=7e8e165bda60d4bc84d665c89ace8752e0e7d6bf CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above."}]},"session_id":"07359a80-925a-4363-b992-bfadc8feb26a"}
